==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 2~8 seconds<sup>60f~240f</sup>.
*1 [[Project A]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Elder Sloth]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[Mistress Celeboodle]]s spawn, delay 0.27~0.67 seconds<sup>8f~20f</sup>.
**1 [[Otta-smack-u]] spawns.
**1 [[Otta-smack-u]] spawns.
**1 [[Otta-smack-u]] spawns.
**9 [[Otta-smack-u]]s spawn, delay 14~26.67 seconds<sup>420f~800f</sup>.
**3 [[Mesocosmocyclone]]s spawn, delay 26.67~33.33 seconds<sup>800f~1,000f</sup>.
**6 [[Mesocosmocyclone]]s spawn, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.

==Strategy==
This stage is pretty easy, especially if you have all [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]]. Use Immune to Warp units such as [[Rover Cat (Rare Cat)|Catellite]], [[Curling Cat (Rare Cat)|Green Shell Cat]] to hold against Mesocosmocyclone. [[Hip Hop Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Can Can Cat]] is also a good choice to chip enemies down, especially if supported by [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]].

In the beginning, only use Catellite to build up some money. Lure and kill Project A before hitting the enemy base. Then just spawn everything you have.

On higher crowns the Mesocosmocyclones will rip apart your defense, so kill them fast using units like [[Wheel Cat (Rare Cat)|Chill Cat]] or [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard]]. Kill the Otta-Smack-Us with [[Ancient Egg: N005 (Special Cat)|Hitman Cat]] or [[Ancient Egg: N111 (Super Rare Cat)|Cop Cat]].

